.TH INSPECT-PROXMOX-HOST-STATUS 8 "2026-09-21" "inspect-proxmox-host" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
inspect-proxmox-host-status \- report the guest egress lockdown's state
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B inspect-proxmox-host-status
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the facts an off-host caller needs to judge whether the guest egress lockdown is
fully in place: the installed contract, whether the marker is present, unit enablement
and result, the default-route interfaces, the mangle-table rules and the SDN dnsmasq
upstream resolver file. Sections are introduced by lines starting with
.B ###
and the report ends with
.BR "### end" .
It never exits non-zero, so a broken host still reports.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR inspect-proxmox-host-seal (8)
